# Answer key for B4 t3_interaction.sql - expressions and types, interaction.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# Conventions: all of B1-B3, plus D-19..D-22.

@ 20 S1 expression GROUP BY key, CASE in SUM, window partitioned by an expression
value fct_order_line.product_key -> product_performance.product_id identity
value fct_order_line.order_date -> product_performance.period_month derived
value fct_order_line.status, fct_order_line.net_amount -> product_performance.revenue aggregated
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> product_performance.revenue_share, product_performance.running_revenue aggregated
influence fct_order_line.product_key, fct_order_line.order_date -> product_performance.revenue, product_performance.revenue_share, product_performance.running_revenue
note GROUP BY keys (D-2), and the windows' PARTITION BY / ORDER BY over the same columns (D-4).
forbid influence fct_order_line.order_date -> product_performance.period_month | a grouping key expression does not influence itself (D-2)
forbid influence fct_order_line.product_key -> product_performance.product_id | a grouping key does not influence itself (D-2)

@ 40 S2 expressions in ON, array and range WHERE, HAVING
value orders.channel -> channel_mix.channel derived
value dim_store.region -> channel_mix.region identity
value orders.id -> channel_mix.orders aggregated
value orders.amount, fx_rates.rate_to_usd -> channel_mix.revenue aggregated
influence orders.channel, dim_store.region -> channel_mix.orders, channel_mix.revenue
filter orders.tags, orders.created_at, orders.updated_at, orders.order_ts -> channel_mix
filter orders.amount, orders.tags -> channel_mix post
forbid filter dim_store.country_code -> channel_mix | an expression in ON is still structural (D-5)
forbid filter orders.currency -> channel_mix | an expression in ON is still structural (D-5)
forbid filter fx_rates.rate_date -> channel_mix | an expression in ON is still structural (D-5)

@ 65 S3 scalar subquery in a CASE test, CASE in a scalar subquery (D-12)
value customers.id -> customer_summary.customer_id identity
value orders.customer_id, customers.id -> customer_summary.status aggregated
note The COUNT(*) subquery's correlation: values of status, aggregated (D-12).
value customers.status -> customer_summary.status conditional
value orders.currency, orders.amount, orders.customer_id, orders.status, customers.id -> customer_summary.avg_basket aggregated
forbid filter orders.status -> customer_summary | a scalar subquery's WHERE decides one value, never which rows land (D-12)
forbid filter customers.id -> customer_summary | a scalar subquery's correlation is a value (D-12)

@ 86 S4 LAG over an aggregate, one-column CASE, named window
value dim_product.product_id -> product_performance.product_id identity
repeat value fct_order_line.order_date -> product_performance.period_month derived
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> product_performance.prev_month_revenue, product_performance.growth_pct aggregated
influence dim_product.product_id, fct_order_line.order_date -> product_performance.prev_month_revenue, product_performance.growth_pct
note Inner GROUP BY keys, and the named window's PARTITION BY / ORDER BY over them (D-4).

@ 111 S5 DISTINCT ON an expression (D-9)
value dim_customer.region -> top_customers.region derived
value dim_customer.customer_id -> top_customers.customer_id identity
value dim_customer.full_name -> top_customers.full_name derived
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> top_customers.revenue identity
filter dim_customer.region, fct_order_line.net_amount -> top_customers
note The DISTINCT ON key and its tie-breaker decide which row survives (D-9).

@ 126 S6 UNION ALL arms, three transforms
value orders.currency -> kpi_rollup.region derived
value orders.amount -> kpi_rollup.revenue identity
filter orders.status -> kpi_rollup
value payments.currency -> kpi_rollup.region identity
value payments.status, payments.amount -> kpi_rollup.revenue conditional
value returns.amount -> kpi_rollup.revenue derived
forbid value returns.amount -> kpi_rollup.revenue conditional | GREATEST(x, 0) is a clamp over one column (D-19)

@ 144 S7 FILTER compounds, string_agg ordered by another column
value dim_carrier.id -> carrier_scorecard.carrier_id identity
value dim_warehouse.region -> carrier_scorecard.carrier_name aggregated
influence dim_warehouse.name -> carrier_scorecard.carrier_name
value fct_shipment.status, fct_shipment.weight_kg -> carrier_scorecard.shipments aggregated
value fct_shipment.cost, fct_shipment.transit_days, fct_shipment.weight_kg -> carrier_scorecard.cost_per_kg aggregated
influence dim_carrier.id, dim_carrier.name -> carrier_scorecard.carrier_name, carrier_scorecard.shipments, carrier_scorecard.cost_per_kg
forbid filter fct_shipment.status -> carrier_scorecard | FILTER (WHERE) changes one aggregate, not the rows (D-10)
forbid filter fct_shipment.transit_days -> carrier_scorecard | FILTER (WHERE) changes one aggregate, not the rows (D-10)

@ 160 S8 RANK over SUM with an expression partition; precision from an aggregate
value fct_order_line.order_date -> sales_daily.sale_date identity
value fct_order_line.store_id -> sales_daily.store_id identity
value dim_store.region -> sales_daily.region identity
influence dim_store.region, fct_order_line.order_date, fct_order_line.net_amount, fct_order_line.store_id -> sales_daily.rank_in_region
note region and date_part(order_date) partition the rank; net_amount orders it through SUM; the GROUP BY keys decide each SUM.
value fct_order_line.net_amount, dim_store.country_code -> sales_daily.avg_order_value aggregated
note The precision MAX(length(country_code)) is a parameter: a value (D-22), aggregated on its path.
influence fct_order_line.order_date, fct_order_line.store_id, dim_store.region -> sales_daily.avg_order_value
forbid value fct_order_line.net_amount -> sales_daily.rank_in_region | RANK's ORDER BY decides the rank; no part of the sum is in it (D-4)
forbid influence dim_store.region -> sales_daily.region | a grouping key does not influence itself (D-2)

@ 182 S9 band CASE over an aggregate, filtered on the band
value dim_customer.region -> kpi_rollup.region identity
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> kpi_rollup.revenue, kpi_rollup.level aggregated
influence dim_customer.region -> kpi_rollup.revenue, kpi_rollup.level
filter fct_order_line.net_amount -> kpi_rollup post
